## Deviations from Plan

None.

## Risks

1. Keycode 84 for slash key - This is the standard Linux keycode for the forward slash key on US keyboards. If the user has a different keyboard layout, the keybinding may not work correctly.
2. The window size formula `(monitor_w*0.4) (monitor_w*0.3)` produces a 4:3 ratio on the current 1920x1080 monitor (768x576), which is smaller than expected. A larger size like `(monitor_w*0.5) (monitor_w*0.375)` would be 960x720.

